  "slug": "eurofurence",
  "name": "Eurofurence",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Eurofurence (EF) is an annual European furry convention and the longest-running furry convention in the world, established in 1995. It is organized by Eurofurence e.V. and is the largest furry convention outside the United States, ranking among the ten largest worldwide, with 9,139 attendees in 2026. The first edition was held June 30 to July 3, 1995, on a vacation farm at Kaiser-Wilhelm-Koog in Germany with 19 participants. Early editions moved between youth hostels and camps in Germany, Sweden, the Netherlands and the Czech Republic, followed by Nuremberg Castle, the Ringberg Hotel in Suhl (2007 to 2009), the Maritim Hotel in Magdeburg (2010 to 2013), the Estrel Hotel in Berlin (2014 to 2022) and the Congress Center Hamburg since 2023. Eurofurence has a guest of honour almost every year since 1999, and each edition has a theme. It also produces EF Prime, an on-site TV channel launched in 2007, and the Daily Eurofurence newspaper.",
